The 10,000-node network evaluations (branch `origin/docs/overhead-eval-10k`,
`docs/eval/*.md`) report how much topic traffic individual registrars receive. They
ran on **older code** (topdisc with the PRs listed in the reports, July 2026), so they
are used here only as load levels. The extracted figures, each with its source and a
verbatim quote, are in `docs/registrar-overhead/inputs/eval10k.csv`;
`inputs/eval10k-README.md` lists what the reports do not contain.

{{if:table:eval10k}}{{table:eval10k}}

"Figure reading" rows were read off the per-message-type packet plots, because the
report text gives REGTOPIC load only in bytes. They are approximate.
{{if:eval10k.hot_5_busy}}
**Placement.** At the hottest registrar of the 5-topic run (about
{{eval10k.rt_hot_5|f:0}} REGTOPIC/s and {{eval10k.tq_hot_5|f:1}} TOPICQUERY/s), the full REGTOPIC cost
of §6.1 (validation included, {{share.cgo.total_ns|sig:2}} ns) and the lookup cost at 25%
occupancy ({{occ.lookup.N250.ns|f:0}} ns) add up to {{eval10k.hot_5_busy|pct:2}} of one core. For the
single-topic run the figure is {{eval10k.hot_1_busy|pct:3}}.{{if:eval10k.knee_over_hot5}} The realtime knee
(§6.4.2) is {{eval10k.knee_over_hot5|sig:2}} times the hottest registrar's request rate.{{endif}}
A typical registrar (the far distance bin) receives
{{eval10k.tq_far_1|f:2}} TOPICQUERY/s and almost no REGTOPIC.{{endif}}

**Missing from the 10k reports:** a per-registrar REGTOPIC rate stated as a number;
distributions across registrars (p50/p99); ad-cache occupancy per registrar and the
cache capacity used; any CPU, memory or latency measurement; commit hashes of the
builds. The registrar loads above therefore cannot be matched to an occupancy, and the
placement assumes the equilibrium occupancy of §6.2.
{{else}}*The 10k input file was not found; no placement is made.*{{endif}}
